.Dd May 16, 2026
.Dt MAPED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm maped
.Nd configure MAP-E Customer Edge state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 1dfp
.Op Fl i Ar seconds
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Op Ar config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
watches DHCPv6 MAP-E lease state and configures the local Customer Edge
runtime.
When lease data changes, or when the configured runtime state differs,
.Nm
runs
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-up
to configure the
.Xr gif 4
interface,
.Xr pf 4
anchor, and IPv4 default route.
.Pp
The helper programs are installed under
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped
and are not intended as the primary user interface.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 1
Run once and exit nonzero if provisioning or configuration fails.
.It Fl d
Run as a daemon.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground.
.It Fl i Ar seconds
Set the polling or health-check interval.
The default is 30 seconds.
.It Fl l Ar level
Set the log level.
Valid values are
.Cm debug ,
.Cm info ,
and
.Cm warn .
.It Fl p
Force polling instead of
.Xr kqueue 2 .
.El
.Pp
If
.Ar config
is not specified,
.Nm
reads
.Pa /etc/maped.conf .
.Pp
External commands are limited to 30 seconds and 1 MiB of captured output.
Timed-out helper process groups are terminated.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The daemon and helpers accept the same literal shell-style assignments.
Values may be unquoted, single-quoted, or double-quoted.
Comments outside quotes are supported.
Variable expansion, command substitution, escapes, and shell commands
are rejected; use explicit values instead.
Restart the daemon after editing configuration.
It passes a frozen, safely quoted configuration to each helper,
so an edit cannot change only half of an operation.
The following variables are commonly set:
.Bl -tag -width PF_ANCHOR_FILE
.It Va WAN_IF
IPv6 WAN interface.
.It Va LEASE_IF
Interface passed to
.Xr dhcp6leasectl 8 .
.It Va LAN_NET
IPv4 LAN network or table expression used in generated
.Xr pf 4
rules.
.It Va GIF_IF
.Xr gif 4
interface to create.
.It Va GIF_MTU
MTU assigned to
.Va GIF_IF .
The default,
.Cm auto ,
uses the current
.Va WAN_IF
MTU minus the 40-byte IPv6 encapsulation header each time the helper runs.
The route to the border relay must use that WAN interface.
A numeric value overrides automatic selection.
The result must be in the
.Xr gif 4
range 1280 through 8192; otherwise the helper fails before changing interfaces.
The generated anchor clamps IPv4 TCP MSS to this MTU minus 40.
For a PPPoE MTU of 1492, these values are 1452 and 1412 respectively.
This is initial interface sizing, not tunnel path MTU discovery.
Health checks recompute it when the WAN MTU changes.
This does not discover smaller downstream links.
Use a lower explicit MTU when the path requires it.
.It Va LEASE_FILE
Optional lease file used only as a change notification trigger.
Persisted lease contents do not authorize service.
The daemon queries current
.Xr dhcp6leasectl 8
state with
.Fl l Fl m
and requires an exact remaining lifetime.
Install the matching patched control utility before upgrading maped.
.It Va PF_ANCHOR_FILE
Path used to store the generated
.Xr pf 4
anchor.
.It Va MAPED_UP
Runtime configuration helper.
.It Va MAPED_DOWN
Ownership-aware withdrawal helper.
.It Va MAPED_DERIVE
MAP-E parameter derivation helper.
.It Va MAPED_STATE_DIR
Directory used for daemon state.
.It Va MAPED_PEER_IPV4
Peer address used on the
.Xr gif 4
interface.
.It Va MAPED_LOG_LEVEL
Log level for
.Nm .
.El
.Pp
Confirmed withdrawal or expiry removes the owned MAP-E configuration.
A temporary control-query failure retains service only until the last
confirmed monotonic deadline.
After restart, a failed query retires previously recorded ownership because
there is no in-memory proof that the old lease remains valid.
The state directory must be owned by root and not writable by other users.
Only one daemon may own it at a time.
Reserve the configured GIF interface and the mape PF anchor for this daemon.
Cleanup deletes the default route only when it still belongs to the recorded
tunnel, and removes the CE alias only when maped originally added it.
Legacy lease.state files alone are not ownership records.
.Sh STATUS AND HISTORY
.Nm
atomically publishes
.Pa status.json
in
.Va MAPED_STATE_DIR
(default
.Pa /var/db/maped )
on each reconciliation cycle and during application and withdrawal.
The file uses base Perl's JSON::PP and requires no additional packages.
It is root-readable and is not used to authorize service or establish ownership.
.Pp
Schema version 1 includes a UTC
.Cm last-update
field, current status, live confirmation and estimated expiry timestamps,
the applied IPv4 address, CE and BR IPv6 addresses, delegated prefix,
and all inclusive TCP/UDP port ranges.
Only active or temporarily degraded service advertises an allocation.
Consumers must check freshness: a stopped daemon or failed write can leave an
old file behind, including after a one-shot invocation.
.Pp
The persistent
.Cm record
array records successfully applied allocation changes, including PSID-only
changes, with UTC
.Cm first-seen
and
.Cm last-seen
observation dates.
Unchanged healthy observations update the last record instead of appending.
History survives restart and withdrawal, is not automatically pruned, and
cannot reconstruct changes while the daemon was stopped.
These dates are observations, not exact ISP assignment times.
Invalid history stops startup rather than silently discarding records.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-derive -compact
.It Pa /etc/maped.conf
Configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/maped
Daemon control script.
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/maped
Daemon.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-up
Runtime configuration helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-down
Runtime teardown helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-derive
MAP-E parameter derivation helper.
.It Pa /var/db/maped/status.json
Atomic JSON status and persistent allocation history (mode 0600).
.It Pa /var/db/maped/lease.state
Default lease state cache.
.It Pa /etc/pf.anchors/mape
Default generated
.Xr pf 4
anchor file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr gif 4 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr pf.conf 5 ,
.Xr dhcp6leasectl 8 ,
.Xr dhcp6leased 8 ,
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
.Xr rcctl 8
